answers.raw_output:
Implement a token‑refresh callback that contains the logic to obtain a new auth token and returns it, e.g.:

```swift
func getRefreshedToken() -> String {
    // Your logic to refresh and return a new auth token
    return refreshedAuthToken
}
```  
The SDK will automatically invoke this callback when it detects an expired token — on any 401 Unauthorized response, before the token’s expiration if it is detected, and on SDK initialization if the stored token is already expired [chunk: unknown:OMNUMI_SDK_IOS_DOCUMENTATION:structural:74].  

Internally, the SDK also monitors the token’s lifetime (the access token is valid for 3600 seconds) and proactively attempts a refresh after 80 % of that lifetime has elapsed (about 48 minutes), running the refresh on a background thread so it does not block in‑flight calls [chunk: v3:auth:structural:1].  

If the callback returns an invalid or expired token, the refresh will fail; ensure it returns a fresh, valid token [chunk: unknown:OMNUMI_SDK_IOS_DOCUMENTATION:structural:122].

